{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"likable-waterworn-willet","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nStory gunshy-symmetric-barnacle (bf96-5776-6a97-420f) moves the reconciler from `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` to `src/rebar/reconciler/`. The ruff per-file ignore that exempts the reconciler's operational `print()` output from T201 is `\"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/*\" = [\"T201\"]` in `pyproject.toml` (`[tool.ruff.lint.per-file-ignores]`, line 567 on origin/main c0cf1022671), and its glob no longer matches anything after the move. Any edit to `pyproject.toml` counts as touching the dependency map, so the Gerrit pip-audit lane (`scripts/dependency_audit.py::touches_dependency_map`, \"if you touch it, you own it\") blocks such a change on the advisories open under unhelpful-supersmart-chrysalis (f7dc-132b-057a-476c). Following the operator's decision on change 3038 (leave `pyproject.toml` untouched, file the stale-line cleanup as a follow-up), the move story leaves `pyproject.toml` alone and puts an inline `# noqa: T201` on each reconciler `print()` site (100 sites in 33 files, added with `ruff check --select T201 --add-noqa src/rebar/reconciler`).\n\n## Approach\n1. In `pyproject.toml`, replace `\"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/*\" = [\"T201\"]` with `\"src/rebar/reconciler/**\" = [\"T201\"]`, and update the comments that name the old path (`:14`, `:68`, `:509`, `:627-634`).\n2. Remove the inline `# noqa: T201` markers from `src/rebar/reconciler/**`, leaving every other noqa code on those lines intact.\n3. Land it only after unhelpful-supersmart-chrysalis closes (the lane stops blocking), or bundle it into the change that remediates those advisories, since that change already owns `uv.lock`/`pyproject.toml`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `grep -n 'rebar_reconciler' pyproject.toml` prints nothing.\n- [ ] `git grep -c 'noqa: T201' -- src/rebar/reconciler` prints nothing.\n- [ ] `ruff check --select T201 src/rebar/reconciler` reports no findings, and `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] The Gerrit pip-audit lane passes on the change.","id":"ab45-2cb2-c1b6-4c5b","parent_id":"ebf5-5d21-0124-4313","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Move the T201 per-file ignore glob from `_engine/rebar_reconciler/*` to `reconciler/*` and drop the inline noqa once the lock advisories clear"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1792424808735150306,"uuid":"ca03ba3c-5ced-4574-8784-bd7b8332f671"}